Package: fusionpep
Type: Project
Title: FusionPep: Peptide Mapping and Junction Review
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Enes K.", "Ergin", email = "eneskemalergin@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9810-7399")),
    person("Agustina", "Conrrero", role = "aut"),
    person("Philipp F.", "Lange", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1171-5864"))
    )
Description: Maps peptide sequences supplied directly or from peptide-spectrum
    match (PSM) exports to a proposed fusion protein and its two selected
    parent proteins. It reports mapped occurrences, parent sharing, residue
    coverage, and pairwise fusion-to-parent alignments. When junction
    coordinates are supplied, it checks whether an occurrence crosses a
    junction and meets the required minimum flank length on both sides. Runs
    write CSV tables, an RDS file containing the analysis result, figures, and
    an HTML report. FusionPep does not search spectra, validate PSMs, establish
    peptide detection, or prove biological fusion expression.
